{"companyInfo": {"Updated": "6/3/26", "Footnote": "Market value as of March 31, 2026.", "Country/Territory": "U.S.", "Headquarters": "Houston", "Industry": "Oil and Gas Equipment, Services", "CEO": "Jeffrey A. Miller", "Website": "https://www.halliburton.com", "Ticker": "HAL", "Company type": "Public", "Revenues ($M)": "$22,184", "Profits ($M)": "$1,283", "Market value ($M)": "$32,563", "Number of employees": "46,000", "StockQuote": "NYSE"}, "description": "Founded in 1919 by Erle P. Halliburton, a pioneer in oil well cementing, Halliburton is a global provider of products and services to the energy industry. Halliburton is considered one of the big three global oilfield services firms along with SLB and Baker Hughes. It operates through two main segments: completion and production, and drilling and evaluation. The completion and production segment specializes in production enhancement, cementing, sand control, and well intervention services, while the drilling and evaluation segment focuses on drilling fluid systems, directional drilling, wireline and perforating, and advanced digital solutions. Halliburton is widely viewed as the U.S. leader in hydraulic fracturing completions, better known as fracking. Halliburton\u2019s technological innovations include achieving the world\u2019s first closed-loop, autonomous fracturing operation, and pioneering AI tools that optimize exploration, drilling, and production workflows. Its DS365.ai platform enables data management, scalable AI/ML model deployment, and app development.", "dataTables": [{"changeHeader": "% change", "footnote": "", "title": "Key Financials (last Fiscal Year)", "valueHeader": "$ millions", "values": [{"change": "-3.3%", "title": "Revenues ($M)", "value": "$22,184"}, {"change": "-48.7%", "title": "Profits ($M)", "value": "$1,283"}, {"change": "-", "title": "Assets ($M)", "value": "$25,010"}, {"change": "-", "title": "Total Stockholder Equity ($M)", "value": "$10,461"}]}, {"changeHeader": "", "footnote":